WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:07.100
SPEAKER: Cloud Spanner is
unique in the marketplace

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.140
because it combines
both relational database

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.210
structure with horizontal
scale and performance.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:14.510
What this means is
that this significantly

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:16.940
simplifies application
development and database

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.900
management, allowing you to
deliver your apps faster.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.780
For example, for globally
distributed apps,

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:26.090
Cloud Spanner's
multi-regional configuration

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:29.420
automatically replicates a
database across continents,

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:33.080
allowing for localized
reads, minimizing latency.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:36.020
Creating or scaling such a
globally replicated database

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.840
only takes a handful of
clicks on the console.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.570
At Google, we use Cloud
Spanner for our own mission

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:44.630
critical services and apps
that billions of people

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:46.910
across the world
access every day,

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:49.340
so downtime just
isn't an option.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:52.100
This hands-on lab shows you
how to create a Cloud Spanner

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:55.980
instance, database, and
table, add a schema,

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.680
write and modify
data, and run a query.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:01.580
Cloud Spanner is ideal for
relational, structured,

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.530
and semi-structured
data that requires

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:07.040
high availability, strong
consistency, and transactional

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.270
reads and writes.

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:11.070
Next up on our quest is
the Internet of Things--

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.920
Qwik Start.

